=== layout: one-panel

# *Deletion Quiz Question*

@body

- [Step 4\: Analyze the deletions that contain only one of the two unordered genes (AC)]{color=red}
  - [Del#1 C, D;]{color=#800080}
  - Del#2 A, C, D;
  - [Del#3 A, B, C;]{color=#B2B2B2}
  - [Hint\: the first gene on the end is gene B.]{color=#B2B2B2}
- B (AC) \_

=== layout: one-panel

# *Deletion Quiz Question*

@body

- [Step 4\: Analyze the deletions that contain only one of the two unordered genes (AC)]{color=red}
  - [Del#1 C, D;]{color=#800080}
  - Del#2 A, C, D;
  - [Del#3 A, B, C;]{color=#B2B2B2}
  - [Hint\: the first gene on the end is gene B.]{color=#B2B2B2}
- Del#1 tells us that C is next to a unassigned gene, and must be on the end away from B
- B (AC) \_

